#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# booleans

#% text
# `booleans` is the domain of the truth values `true` and `false`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `element(x, booleans)` is `true` for `true` and `false`, `false` for numbers and strings, and stays unevaluated for a symbol.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
element(true, booleans)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(0, booleans)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
element(x, booleans)
#% output
#= element(x, booleans)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `element`, `integers`, `reals`
